<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="012" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>B-4b thread ICallerContext through decision slice</title>
    <phase>A BFF rework</phase>
    <gate>after 010 and 011</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags include bff-api; modifies 9 existing .cs files; refactor</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Cross-cutting refactor across 9 existing files (Risk Register R10, confirmed high probability) on the caller path of every decision write</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>B</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Shares no file with 002; serial with 017/013/014 through deps (Services/Signals/** chain)</parallel-reason>
    <deps>010, 011</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, refactoring, integration-test, unit-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Remove HttpContext and IHttpContextAccessor from the decision slice's executors, route cores, notifier and stamp by threading ICallerContext through DecisionPlanReadStamp, Actions/DecisionParameterSources, Actions/DecisionActionExecutors, Actions/DecisionRouteCores, AssignTaskNotifier, DecisionCommitFollowUps and Actions/BudgetInquiryExecutor, with behaviour unchanged, and add an ArchTest guard that keeps HttpContext out of Services/Signals/**.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in large C# refactors with strict behaviour preservation.</role>
  <goal>The seven files take no HttpContext or IHttpContextAccessor; a source-scan guard enforces it for Services/Signals/** with a ratchet baseline holding only DecisionCommitService.cs (emptied by 014); all existing Signals tests and 011's baselines pass unchanged.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Pipeline discovery (project CLAUDE.md §6 gotcha): HttpContext reaches DecisionPlanReadStamp L42/L86, DecisionParameterSources L109/L404, DecisionActionExecutors (record field HttpContext Http L73), DecisionRouteCores (7 methods), AssignTaskNotifier (5), DecisionCommitFollowUps L70 and BudgetInquiryExecutor (IHttpContextAccessor). FR-10 requires none of the decision-slice methods to take HttpContext. DecisionCommitService's own HttpContext parameters (L439, L622, L770, L927, L1578) are removed in 014.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/DecisionPlanReadStamp.cs (L42, L86)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/Actions/DecisionParameterSources.cs (L109, L404)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/Actions/DecisionActionExecutors.cs (record field HttpContext Http, L73)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/Actions/DecisionRouteCores.cs (7 methods)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/AssignTaskNotifier.cs (5 methods)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/DecisionCommitFollowUps.cs (L70)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/Actions/BudgetInquiryExecutor.cs (IHttpContextAccessor)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/DecisionCommitService.cs (ONLY the call sites that build DecisionActionRequest, L1966, or call the changed methods)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Signals/DecisionPlanEndpoints.cs (ONLY the call sites of the changed stamp/parameter-source methods)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/DecisionSliceHttpContextGuardTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Authentication/ICallerContext.cs (from 010)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs (source-scan guard style, must-fire/must-not-fire controls)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="010" status="pending">ICallerContext and the fail-closed Dataverse client</dependency>
      <dependency task="011" status="pending">REST contract baselines that must stay green</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Behaviour is unchanged: every edit replaces where the caller comes from (HttpContext → ICallerContext) and nothing else; no statement reordering, no new branch, no changed message or reason code.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Every operation this task adds or changes reads the caller only from ICallerContext (task 010); an unpopulated context returns DataverseUserClientErrorCodes.UserContextRequired (DATAVERSE_USER_CONTEXT_REQUIRED) and never falls back to an app-only client (FR-10, ADR-002 WP-6 fail closed).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">In every file this task touches, SignalReadService read rules and DecisionCommitService validation, idempotency and execution order are unchanged; DecisionCommitService stays the single owner of completion; SignalWriter, DecisionRecordWriter and DecisionCallerRights are not edited.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">The REST responses of GET /api/v1/signals/worklist, GET /api/v1/signals/{id}/decision-plan, GET /api/v1/signals/{id}/suppression and POST /api/v1/signals/{id}/decision stay byte-for-byte unchanged: task 011's contract baseline tests pass with no golden-file edit (FR-09).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Existing tests change only in constructor or DI wiring; each changed test file is listed in the PR with the reason; no expected value changes (FAILURE-MODES AP-9).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The new guard ships with a must-fire control (a fixture source declaring an HttpContext parameter fails) and a must-not-fire control, and a ratchet baseline listing only DecisionCommitService.cs (root CLAUDE.md §16 enforcement ladder).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">T170's per-commit WhoAmI count stays 1 and #2580's 'one batched BillingEventRead per worklist response' assertion stays green.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Every PR from this task that touches Services/Signals/**, Api/Signals/** or the worklist route is reviewed by spaarke-ontology-platform-r1 before merge (project CLAUDE.md §4); run /conflict-check before opening it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Every change this task makes under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ is listed in the PR with a Placement Justification that cites .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (source text: spec.md 'Placement Justification'), and the PR records the publish-size delta against a fresh master build per .claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md 'BFF Publish-Size Per-Task Verification Rule': a delta of +5 MB or more needs explicit justification, a total of 55 MB or more triggers architecture review, and the total must stay at or under 60 MB (hard stop). No new HIGH CVE (dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Every test this task adds lives on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,contract,regression,data-mutation}/** or tests/unit/domain/**), mocks only at module boundaries, and uses no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; or Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Any defect found and not fixed in this task is filed with /project-defer-issue-tracking (notes/defer-issues.md AND a GitHub issue), never one without the other (project CLAUDE.md §2).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-definition.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/unit-test-structure.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/mocking-patterns.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-002-thin-plugins.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-010-di-minimalism.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-029-bff-publish-hygiene.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/pre-pipeline-context.md</file>
      <file>.claude/FAILURE-MODES.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">For each of the seven files, list every HttpContext/IHttpContextAccessor use and what it reads (caller, token, correlation id, or anything else).</step>
    <step order="2">Replace each use with ICallerContext (constructor-injected for scoped services; a field on DecisionActionRequest in place of HttpContext Http).</step>
    <step order="3">Update only the call sites in DecisionCommitService.cs and DecisionPlanEndpoints.cs that the signature changes force.</step>
    <step order="4">Add DecisionSliceHttpContextGuardTests: scan Services/Signals/** for parameters, fields or record members of type HttpContext or IHttpContextAccessor; ratchet baseline = DecisionCommitService.cs only; must-fire and must-not-fire fixtures.</step>
    <step order="5">Run 011's baselines, the Signals data-mutation, regression and integration suites, T170 and Task174_*; list changed test files.</step>
    <step order="6">Measure the publish-size delta; open the PR for ontology review.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="8">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any method reads something from HttpContext other than the caller, bearer token or correlation id (headers, Items, response), STOP and list it rather than inventing a replacement.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a test's expected value (not its wiring) would have to change, STOP and escalate (AP-9).</trigger>
    <trigger>If removing HttpContext from DecisionCommitService call sites would require reordering its steps, STOP: that belongs to 014 under the invariant list.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs scans route mapping, not Services/Signals/** parameter types; no guard for HttpContext in services exists (grep -rln HttpContext tests/Spaarke.ArchTests returns no service-layer guard).</existing>
    <extension>No: RouteAuthorizationGuardTests checks endpoint authorization metadata, a different rule; adding parameter-type scanning there would mix two guards in one class.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the guard, FR-10's rule lives only in prose and the next decision-slice change can reintroduce HttpContext, making MCP tools fail silently outside a request.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET projects (dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/, dotnet test)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/ (seven files listed above)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/DecisionSliceHttpContextGuardTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">None of the seven listed files declares a parameter, field or record member of type HttpContext or IHttpContextAccessor (guard passes).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">DecisionSliceHttpContextGuardTests: the must-fire fixture fails the guard, the must-not-fire fixture passes, and the ratchet baseline contains only DecisionCommitService.cs.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">011's contract baselines pass with no golden-file change.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Existing Signals tests pass; only constructor/DI wiring changed in test files, each listed in the PR.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: with ICallerContext unpopulated, the BudgetInquiryExecutor path and one DecisionRouteCores path return UserContextRequired and make no Dataverse call (new tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">T170 WhoAmIs == 1; all Task174_* tests pass, including the one-batched-BillingEventRead count.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The PR records the publish-size delta (at or under 60 MB, no new HIGH CVE) and the ontology review.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Plan risk R10. The guard is the enforcement-ladder mechanism for FR-10 (root CLAUDE.md §16); request one seeding proof for it. DecisionCommitService.cs edits are limited to forced call sites; its own HttpContext parameters are 014's.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
